== Twenty-seven national programmes is the wrong answer

The comparative exercise produces one result that no single-country study could: for at
least six member states the national-only model does not close. Estonia, Latvia and
Lithuania cannot place a strategic reserve at a defensible distance from a frontline
border inside their own territory. Cyprus, Malta and Luxembourg cannot meet the
separation guidance at all — Nicosia to Limassol is eighty kilometres, and that is the
island's maximum.

